{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1768790549910,"sessionID":"ses_42bde3593ffewMjoFeBKVAd3J5","part":{"id":"prt_bd421e4a8001fESJptcL3uW36q","sessionID":"ses_42bde3593ffewMjoFeBKVAd3J5","messageID":"msg_bd421ca9d001eH5iRIYzpkqnsX","type":"tool","callID":"call_function_1nsbm3xjrhtl_4","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/smaluk/dev/personal/chronotunes/AGENTS.md"},"output":"<file>\n00001| # AGENTS.md - ChronoTunes\n00002| \n00003| Guidelines for AI coding agents working in this repository.\n00004| \n00005| ## Project Overview\n00006| \n00007| Browser-based multiplayer music timeline game (Hitster clone) with YouTube audio.\n00008| - **Frontend**: Next.js 16 (App Router) + TypeScript\n00009| - **Backend**: Convex (realtime BaaS)\n00010| - **Package Manager**: pnpm\n00011| \n00012| ## Commands\n00013| \n00014| ### Development\n00015| ```bash\n00016| pnpm dev                    # Start Next.js dev server\n00017| just run-local-backend      # Start local Convex backend (Terminal 1)\n00018| just convex dev             # Deploy to local backend (Terminal 2)\n00019| ```\n00020| \n00021| ### Linting & Formatting\n00022| ```bash\n00023| pnpm biome check .          # Lint + format check\n00024| pnpm biome check . --write  # Auto-fix lint + format issues\n00025| pnpm biome format .         # Format only\n00026| ```\n00027| \n00028| ### Type Generation\n00029| ```bash\n00030| pnpm next:typegen           # Generate Next.js types\n00031| pnpm convex:typegen         # Generate Convex types\n00032| ```\n00033| \n00034| ### Testing\n00035| ```bash\n00036| pnpm test                   # Run all tests (vitest)\n00037| pnpm test <file>            # Run single test file\n00038| pnpm test <pattern>         # Run tests matching pattern\n00039| pnpm test --watch           # Watch mode\n00040| pnpm test:integration       # Integration tests against local backend\n00041| ```\n00042| \n00043| ### Pre-Commit (must all pass)\n00044| ```bash\n00045| pnpm biome check .\n00046| pnpm next:typegen\n00047| pnpm convex:typegen\n00048| pnpm test\n00049| ```\n00050| \n00051| ## Code Style\n00052| \n00053| ### Formatting (Biome)\n00054| - **NOT ESLint** - this project uses Biome\n00055| - 2 space indentation\n00056| - Double quotes for strings\n00057| - Semicolons required\n00058| - Trailing commas in multiline\n00059| \n00060| ### Imports\n00061| ```typescript\n00062| // Order: external packages, then internal, then relative\n00063| import { useQuery } from \"convex/react\";\n00064| import { api } from \"@/convex/_generated/api\";\n00065| import { Button } from \"@/components/ui/button\";\n00066| import { GameHeader } from \"./GameHeader\";\n00067| ```\n00068| \n00069| ### TypeScript\n00070| - Strict mode enabled\n00071| - Explicit return types on exported functions\n00072| - Use `type` for object shapes, `interface` for extendable contracts\n00073| - Prefer `unknown` over `any`\n00074| - Use Convex's `Id<\"tableName\">` for document IDs\n00075| \n00076| ```typescript\n00077| // Good\n00078| export function computeValidRange(timeline: TimelineEntry[], year: number): Range {\n00079|   // ...\n00080| }\n00081| \n00082| // Bad - no return type\n00083| export function computeValidRange(timeline: TimelineEntry[], year: number) {\n00084| ```\n00085| \n00086| ### Naming Conventions\n00087| - **Files**: kebab-case (`game-logic.ts`, `betting-panel.tsx`)\n00088| - **Components**: PascalCase (`TimelinePlacer.tsx` exports `TimelinePlacer`)\n00089| - **Functions/variables**: camelCase\n00090| - **Constants**: SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE\n00091| - **Types/Interfaces**: PascalCase\n00092| \n00093| ### React Components\n00094| - One component per `.tsx` file (except `components/ui/`)\n00095| - Extract subcomponents to separate files\n00096| - Use function declarations, not arrow functions for components\n00097| \n00098| ```typescript\n00099| // Good\n00100| export function PlayerCard({ player }: PlayerCardProps) {\n00101|   return <div>...</div>;\n00102| }\n00103| \n00104| // Bad\n00105| export const PlayerCard = ({ player }: PlayerCardProps) => {\n00106|   return <div>...</div>;\n00107| };\n00108| ```\n00109| \n00110| ### Convex Functions\n00111| - Mutations and queries in `convex/*.ts`\n00112| - Pure logic in `convex/lib/*.ts`\n00113| - Use `convex-helpers` sessionWrapper for auth\n00114| \n00115| ```typescript\n00116| // convex/lobbies.ts\n00117| import { mutation, query } from \"./_generated/server\";\n00118| import { v } from \"convex/values\";\n00119| \n00120| export const create = mutation({\n00121|   args: { displayName: v.string() },\n00122|   handler: async (ctx, args) => {\n00123|     // Implementation\n00124|   },\n00125| });\n00126| ```\n00127| \n00128| ### Error Handling\n00129| - Throw `ConvexError` in Convex functions with user-friendly messages\n00130| - Use error boundaries in React for unexpected errors\n00131| - Handle known error states in UI (loading, not found, unauthorized)\n00132| \n00133| ```typescript\n00134| import { ConvexError } from \"convex/values\";\n00135| \n00136| if (!lobby) {\n00137|   throw new ConvexError(\"Lobby not found\");\n00138| }\n00139| ```\n00140| \n00141| ## Testing\n00142| \n00143| ### Test File Location\n00144| Tests live alongside source files:\n00145| ```\n00146| convex/lobbies.ts           → convex/lobbies.test.ts\n00147| convex/lib/gameLogic.ts     → convex/lib/gameLogic.test.ts\n00148| components/game/Timer.tsx   → components/game/Timer.test.tsx\n00149| ```\n00150| \n00151| ### Convex Function Tests\n00152| ```typescript\n00153| import { convexTest } from \"convex-test\";\n00154| import { expect, test } from \"vitest\";\n00155| import { api } from \"./_generated/api\";\n00156| import schema from \"./schema\";\n00157| \n00158| test(\"create lobby generates 6-char code\", async () => {\n00159|   const t = convexTest(schema);\n00160|   const result = await t.mutation(api.lobbies.create, { displayName: \"Host\" });\n00161|   expect(result.code).toHaveLength(6);\n00162| });\n00163| ```\n00164| \n00165| ### Component Tests\n00166| ```typescript\n00167| import { render, screen } from \"@testing-library/react\";\n00168| import { expect, test, vi } from \"vitest\";\n00169| import { PlayerCard } from \"./PlayerCard\";\n00170| \n00171| test(\"displays player name\", () => {\n00172|   render(<PlayerCard player={{ displayName: \"Alice\", coins: 3 }} />);\n00173|   expect(screen.getByText(\"Alice\")).toBeInTheDocument();\n00174| });\n00175| ```\n00176| \n00177| ## Project Structure\n00178| \n00179| ```\n00180| app/\n00181|   [locale]/               # i18n locale segment (en, es, fr, de, pt, ja)\n00182|     page.tsx              # Landing page\n00183|     lobby/[code]/page.tsx # Lobby + game view\n00184|     layout.tsx            # Locale layout with NextIntlClientProvider\n00185|   layout.tsx              # Root layout\n00186|   providers.tsx           # Context providers\n00187| \n00188| components/\n00189|   ui/                     # shadcn/ui components (multi-component files OK)\n00190|   lobby/                  # Lobby-specific components\n00191|   game/                   # Game-specific components\n00192|   player/                 # YouTube player wrapper\n00193| \n00194| convex/\n00195|   schema.ts               # Database schema\n00196|   lib/                    # Pure logic (sessionWrapper, gameLogic)\n00197|   lobbies.ts              # Lobby mutations/queries\n00198|   players.ts              # Player mutations/queries\n00199|   games.ts                # Game mutations/queries\n00200|   rounds.ts               # Round mutations/queries\n00201|   bets.ts                 # Betting mutations/queries\n00202|   tracks.ts               # Track queries\n00203| \n00204| i18n/\n00205|   request.ts              # getRequestConfig for next-intl\n00206|   routing.ts              # Locale routing config (defineRouting)\n00207| \n00208| messages/\n00209|   en.json                 # English translations (default)\n00210|   es.json                 # Spanish\n00211|   fr.json                 # French\n00212|   de.json                 # German\n00213|   pt.json                 # Portuguese\n00214|   ja.json                 # Japanese\n00215| \n00216| lib/\n00217|   session.ts              # Client sessionId (localStorage)\n00218|   hooks/                  # Custom React hooks\n00219| ```\n00220| \n00221| ## UI Stack\n00222| \n00223| - **Tailwind CSS v4.1** with fluid-tailwindcss\n00224| - **shadcn/ui**: Lyra style, Neutral base, Fuchsia theme\n00225| - **Icons**: Lucide\n00226| - **Theming**: next-themes (light/dark)\n00227| - **Toasts**: sonner\n00228| - **i18n**: next-intl (internationalization)\n00229| \n00230| ## Key Patterns\n00231| \n00232| ### Session Management\n00233| ```typescript\n00234| // Client: lib/session.ts\n00235| export function getSessionId(): string {\n00236|   let id = localStorage.getItem(\"sessionId\");\n00237|   if (!id) {\n00238|     id = crypto.randomUUID();\n00239|     localStorage.setItem(\"sessionId\", id);\n00240|   }\n00241|   return id;\n00242| }\n00243| ```\n00244| \n00245| ### Convex Queries\n00246| ```typescript\n00247| // Decoupled queries - don't fetch everything in one query\n00248| const lobby = useQuery(api.lobbies.get, { code });\n00249| const players = useQuery(api.players.list, lobby ? { lobbyId: lobby._id } : \"skip\");\n00250| const me = useQuery(api.players.getMe, lobby ? { lobbyId: lobby._id } : \"skip\");\n00251| ```\n00252| \n00253| ### Real-time State\n00254| All game state lives in Convex. No client-side state management library.\n00255| Convex subscriptions handle real-time updates automatically.\n00256| \n00257| ## Internationalization (next-intl)\n00258| \n00259| ### File Structure\n00260| ```\n00261| i18n/\n00262|   request.ts          # getRequestConfig\n00263|   routing.ts          # defineRouting with locales\n00264| messages/\n00265|   en.json             # English (default)\n00266|   es.json             # Spanish\n00267|   fr.json             # French\n00268|   de.json             # German\n00269|   pt.json             # Portuguese\n00270|   ja.json             # Japanese\n00271| ```\n00272| \n00273| ### Translation Keys\n00274| Use nested namespaces matching component structure:\n00275| ```json\n00276| {\n00277|   \"common\": {\n00278|     \"loading\": \"Loading...\",\n00279|     \"error\": \"An error occurred\"\n00280|   },\n00281|   \"lobby\": {\n00282|     \"title\": \"Game Lobby\",\n00283|     \"joinCode\": \"Join Code\",\n00284|     \"startGame\": \"Start Game\"\n00285|   },\n00286|   \"game\": {\n00287|     \"round\": \"Round {number}\",\n00288|     \"yourTurn\": \"Your Turn\",\n00289|     \"placeSong\": \"Place this song on your timeline\"\n00290|   }\n00291| }\n00292| ```\n00293| \n00294| ### Using Translations\n00295| ```typescript\n00296| // In Server Components\n00297| import { getTranslations } from \"next-intl/server\";\n00298| \n00299| export default async function LobbyPage() {\n00300|   const t = await getTranslations(\"lobby\");\n00301|   return <h1>{t(\"title\")}</h1>;\n00302| }\n00303| \n00304| // In Client Components\n00305| \"use client\";\n00306| import { useTranslations } from \"next-intl\";\n00307| \n00308| export function StartButton() {\n00309|   const t = useTranslations(\"lobby\");\n00310|   return <Button>{t(\"startGame\")}</Button>;\n00311| }\n00312| ```\n00313| \n00314| ### Linking with Locale\n00315| ```typescript\n00316| import { Link } from \"@/i18n/routing\";\n00317| \n00318| // Automatically preserves current locale\n00319| <Link href=\"/lobby/ABC123\">Join Lobby</Link>\n00320| ```\n00321| \n00322| ### Adding New Translation Keys\n00323| 1. Add key to `messages/en.json` first\n00324| 2. Add same key to all other locale files\n00325| 3. Use `t(\"namespace.key\")` in components\n00326| 4. Never hardcode user-facing strings\n00327| \n00328| ## Don't\n00329| \n00330| - Don't use ESLint (use Biome)\n00331| - Don't use client-side state libraries (Zustand, Redux) - use Convex\n00332| - Don't use `any` type\n00333| - Don't create documentation files unless explicitly requested\n00334| - Don't add emojis unless explicitly requested\n00335| - Don't put multiple components in one file (except `components/ui/`)\n00336| - Don't hardcode user-facing strings (use next-intl translations)\n00337| \n00338| ## Landing the Plane (Session Completion)\n00339| \n00340| **When ending a work session**, you MUST complete ALL steps below. Work is NOT complete until `git push` succeeds.\n00341| \n00342| **MANDATORY WORKFLOW:**\n00343| \n00344| 1. **File issues for remaining work** - Create issues for anything that needs follow-up\n00345| 2. **Run quality gates** (if code changed) - Tests, linters, builds\n00346| 3. **Update issue status** - Close finished work, update in-progress items\n00347| 4. **PUSH TO REMOTE** - This is MANDATORY:\n00348|    ```bash\n00349|    git pull --rebase\n00350|    bd sync\n00351|    git push\n00352|    git status  # MUST show \"up to date with origin\"\n00353|    ```\n00354| 5. **Clean up** - Clear stashes, prune remote branches\n00355| 6. **Verify** - All changes committed AND pushed\n00356| 7. **Hand off** - Provide context for next session\n00357| \n00358| **CRITICAL RULES:**\n00359| - Work is NOT complete until `git push` succeeds\n00360| - NEVER stop before pushing - that leaves work stranded locally\n00361| - NEVER say \"ready to push when you are\" - YOU must push\n00362| - If push fails, resolve and retry until it succeeds\n00363| Use 'bd' for task tracking\n00364| \n\n(End of file - total 364 lines)\n</file>","title":"AGENTS.md","metadata":{"preview":"# AGENTS.md - ChronoTunes\n\nGuidelines for AI coding agents working in this repository.\n\n## Project Overview\n\nBrowser-based multiplayer music timeline game (Hitster clone) with YouTube audio.\n- **Frontend**: Next.js 16 (App Router) + TypeScript\n- **Backend**: Convex (realtime BaaS)\n- **Package Manager**: pnpm\n\n## Commands\n\n### Development\n```bash\npnpm dev      